The experiment is done on an unusual time in Fugaku when point-to-point communication was performing
abysmally bad and the results were not matching the results of previous experiments on same input
and parameter configurations for either the reference program and the HighP5 program versions. So we
have to drastically reduce the number of iterations and increase the amount of padding in the upper
layer to dampen the impact of highly costly MPI point-to-point communications.

